WEBVTT

04:09.708 --> 04:10.834
Kneel.

04:15.464 --> 04:17.590
I can make it clean, or...

04:17.591 --> 04:19.759
Might I at least know
the accusation, my prince?

04:19.760 --> 04:21.052
Where is he?

04:21.845 --> 04:23.721
- Who?
- My brother, the king.

04:23.722 --> 04:24.931
In his quarters!

04:26.099 --> 04:28.434
You are a traitor to the crown.

04:28.435 --> 04:30.144
- I sentence you to die.
- No!

04:30.145 --> 04:31.688
My prince.

04:32.689 --> 04:35.776
It appears Lord Larys
has fled the Keep as well.

04:39.237 --> 04:40.155
Mm.

04:50.916 --> 04:53.125
I need milk of the poppy.

04:53.126 --> 04:56.128
I'm afraid in our hasty flight
that I neglected to bring any.

04:56.129 --> 04:57.922
Ah, the pain!

04:57.923 --> 05:00.217
Please. Please.

05:01.927 --> 05:03.220
Take heart, my king.

05:04.387 --> 05:05.931
These are dark hours, but...

05:07.182 --> 05:09.058
brighter days lie ahead.

05:09.059 --> 05:11.353
No. No.

05:13.146 --> 05:14.731
I'm the king of nothing.

05:15.982 --> 05:20.153
With raven shit for a throne
and a cripple for a protector.

05:21.238 --> 05:23.240
Oh, I'm fucking pathetic.

05:27.160 --> 05:28.495
Oh, fuck!

05:32.958 --> 05:34.376
Draw your hood.

05:52.310 --> 05:53.687
Wait, no, wait!

05:59.693 --> 06:01.318
Who are you?

06:01.319 --> 06:03.238
Simple men in service of the Citadel.

06:05.115 --> 06:07.241
We're taking these ravens to White Harbor.

06:07.242 --> 06:09.326
You're in the queen's lands.

06:09.327 --> 06:13.497
If you mean to pass,
you first have to denounce the usurper,

06:13.498 --> 06:15.124
bend the knee.

06:15.125 --> 06:20.881
You swear fealty to Her Grace,
the one true queen, Rhaenyra Targaryen.

06:25.468 --> 06:27.595
We denounce the usurper

06:27.596 --> 06:30.640
and swear to Her Grace,
Rhaenyra Targaryen.

06:36.646 --> 06:37.480
Come on, friend.

06:38.148 --> 06:40.317
Affirm your fealty
so we might be on our way.

06:44.905 --> 06:46.614
The captain said kneel.

06:46.615 --> 06:47.949
Fuck you.

06:54.539 --> 06:56.082
Forgive my friend, he can be so stubborn.

06:56.833 --> 06:58.043
They're for Aegon.

06:58.877 --> 07:00.753
Put them to the sword.

07:00.754 --> 07:02.756
- Wait, please. Please.
- It's a very lucky day for you, my lord.

07:05.133 --> 07:08.970
The reason this man won't swear
fealty to Rhaenyra...

07:11.681 --> 07:13.725
is because he is Aegon Targaryen.

07:16.102 --> 07:17.103
What?

07:17.604 --> 07:19.939
No, no, that's--

07:19.940 --> 07:22.816
What are you playing at, friend?
Always jesting.

07:22.817 --> 07:24.693
- That true?
- No.

07:24.694 --> 07:27.404
No, of course not.
These are lies.

07:27.405 --> 07:29.782
He was lustrated in dragonfire
by Rhaenys Targaryen...

07:29.783 --> 07:30.741
- No.
- ...and her dragon

07:30.742 --> 07:31.867
at the Battle of Rook's Rest.

07:31.868 --> 07:33.702
My companion is always the gifted mummer.

07:33.703 --> 07:36.121
- I am His Grace's loyal councillor...
- Always making grand claims

07:36.122 --> 07:37.414
- for his entertainment.
- ...and the Lord of Harrenhal--

07:37.415 --> 07:39.166
Outrageous fucking lies!

07:39.167 --> 07:40.376
Someone's lying.

07:40.377 --> 07:42.003
- His crown.
- No.

08:01.815 --> 08:03.358
Pretty hair.

08:05.652 --> 08:06.987
Take their heads.

08:07.946 --> 08:10.030
We'll make a rich bounty for the queen.

08:10.031 --> 08:11.240
- Forgive me, my lord...
- No, no, no, please.

08:11.241 --> 08:12.617
...but you would lose
your own head for such a misstep.

08:14.744 --> 08:16.621
This is the challenger himself.

08:18.707 --> 08:20.875
You can name your price
for delivering him...

08:21.876 --> 08:27.257
and his most trusted confidant
to the queen as living hostages.

08:29.467 --> 08:31.051
Who are they, then?

08:31.052 --> 08:32.637
No one of consequence.

08:36.307 --> 08:37.558
What's the nearest port?

08:37.559 --> 08:38.768
Duskendale.

08:40.103 --> 08:41.228
Bar them within.

08:41.229 --> 08:42.522
We'll take them there.

08:43.982 --> 08:45.734
And hire a ship to Dragonstone.

08:48.611 --> 08:50.363
I have to believe...

08:51.990 --> 08:54.159
that Alicent's offer was genuine.

08:55.452 --> 08:58.912
It is a ruse cloaked in stale friendship.

08:58.913 --> 09:01.541
The risk she took in coming here
is beyond question.

09:02.667 --> 09:04.502
And the risk she now asks you to take?

09:07.464 --> 09:12.260
To fly to the Greens' stronghold
based on her word alone.

09:14.679 --> 09:16.514
It is a trap, Mother...

09:17.599 --> 09:21.060
to lure you and Daemon into Vhagar's jaws.

09:21.061 --> 09:25.147
No! Vhagar and Aemond are gone.
They have flown to Harrenhal.

09:25.148 --> 09:28.693
And Aegon is bedridden.

09:37.744 --> 09:40.370
I could take both Aegon and the throne

09:40.371 --> 09:42.081
in a single stroke.

09:42.082 --> 09:43.083
No.

09:44.125 --> 09:46.044
You cannot trust her.

09:48.254 --> 09:49.631
Mother.

09:52.550 --> 09:54.384
Alicent came to Dragonstone.

09:54.385 --> 09:57.471
- Alicent?
- Under a banner of peace.

09:57.472 --> 09:58.764
Surely, this is not possible.

09:58.765 --> 10:01.434
The Greens know already
that their defeat is written.

10:04.062 --> 10:08.608
Aemond flies on Vhagar
to join Cole in the Riverlands.

10:09.567 --> 10:13.487
With him gone, Alicent will open
the gates of the Red Keep

10:13.488 --> 10:15.906
and surrender Aegon to me.

10:15.907 --> 10:18.450
I will then take his head and the throne.

10:18.451 --> 10:20.536
What are her terms, Your Grace?

10:20.537 --> 10:22.996
That she, Helaena,
and Jaehaera are spared,

10:22.997 --> 10:25.624
and that this war ends
without further bloodshed.

10:25.625 --> 10:28.752
That is a low price.
Do you believe she can be trusted?

10:28.753 --> 10:30.838
Get word to Lord Corlys in the Gullet.

10:30.839 --> 10:33.882
I require ships to deliver
fighting men enough to secure the city.

10:33.883 --> 10:35.968
Your Grace, I protest
this action with all my po--

10:35.969 --> 10:37.219
And Daemon must return with haste.

10:37.220 --> 10:38.596
I'll write to him.

10:39.806 --> 10:42.267
We'll fly to King's Landing
in two days' time...

10:43.351 --> 10:45.186
and take the city.

10:55.905 --> 10:58.366
Good morrow, ser. My queen.

10:58.992 --> 11:00.034
The king requires an audience.

11:17.010 --> 11:19.179
Rather to the throne room, Your Grace.

11:33.651 --> 11:34.652
Aemond.

11:40.992 --> 11:42.410
Why are you here?

11:49.792 --> 11:51.419
Aegon has abdicated the throne.

11:53.880 --> 11:55.255
Abdicated? What do you mean?

11:55.256 --> 11:58.468
Fled King's Landing with that toad Larys.

11:59.886 --> 12:02.513
No, Aegon was bedridden.

12:03.514 --> 12:05.349
Where could he have gone? Why?

12:05.350 --> 12:07.560
Because he's even more stupid
than he is craven.

12:08.978 --> 12:11.064
We must send a search party.
He needs to be found immediately.

12:11.648 --> 12:13.608
Where were you, Mother?

12:15.235 --> 12:17.445
You've not been seen in the Keep in days.

12:25.912 --> 12:27.664
I was in the Kingswood, Aemond.

12:28.665 --> 12:30.792
I have found myself
of little use here of late.

12:35.088 --> 12:36.589
And what of Harrenhal?

12:37.632 --> 12:39.925
You and Vhagar were meant to fly
to meet Ser Criston

12:39.926 --> 12:41.469
and challenge Daemon together.

12:43.680 --> 12:46.808
Aegon has left me no choice
but to remain here and defend the city.

12:49.686 --> 12:52.271
But aid is coming.

12:52.272 --> 12:54.606
Lord Ormund and 15,000 Hightower men

12:54.607 --> 12:57.067
presently march up the Mander
with Daeron and his dragon.

12:57.068 --> 12:59.444
And the Triarchy fleet will,
at any moment,

12:59.445 --> 13:02.657
ambush the blockade with a force
thrice the Sea Snake's strength.

13:07.954 --> 13:09.580
We only need to bide our time.

14:45.551 --> 14:47.386
The Lannister host has scattered,
my prince.

14:47.387 --> 14:50.390
The vanguard was smashed
and the rearguard broken and fled.

14:54.394 --> 14:56.270
And what of the golden Lord Lannister?

14:57.313 --> 14:59.231
Fled when the cavalry broke rank.

14:59.232 --> 15:01.942
Our scouts believe they may be
regrouping near the God's Eye.

15:01.943 --> 15:03.443
Then we'll continue the fight there.

15:03.444 --> 15:05.362
We must pursue them till the last.

15:05.363 --> 15:08.698
- Have graves dug for our dead.
- Aye, my lord.

15:08.699 --> 15:10.701
Caraxes would make short work
of these bodies.

15:11.577 --> 15:13.954
And burnt flesh carries no plague.

15:13.955 --> 15:15.997
That is not our way.

15:15.998 --> 15:17.875
Rivermen must be returned to the mud.

15:21.421 --> 15:22.547
My lord!

15:29.595 --> 15:30.555
To arms!

15:31.556 --> 15:32.557
Form on me!

16:43.377 --> 16:47.590
We have come to die for the dragon queen.

16:57.725 --> 17:01.062
Very good.
We've got more lions to hunt.

17:55.825 --> 17:57.410
Good morrow, Lord Hand.

18:00.746 --> 18:02.290
Has there been word from Prince Aemond?

18:03.332 --> 18:05.459
None. As yet.

18:07.545 --> 18:09.087
He and Vhagar were
supposed to have joined us

18:09.088 --> 18:10.423
back at the Antlers.

18:11.882 --> 18:14.551
We march ever exposed.

18:14.552 --> 18:16.387
- If he does not come--
- He has to come.

18:21.309 --> 18:22.727
There is another matter.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.980
One of our men has ravaged a village girl.

18:26.981 --> 18:28.316
I witnessed the events myself.

18:29.900 --> 18:31.319
Something must be done.

18:32.528 --> 18:34.739
Hang him then, if you wish.

18:35.865 --> 18:38.075
I am not his Lord Commander.

18:41.245 --> 18:46.334
A punishment is due, yes,
but also a statement to the men.

18:47.209 --> 18:49.794
That we are not beasts, but knights,

18:49.795 --> 18:51.296
and soldiers of honor.

18:51.297 --> 18:52.882
Look around you, Ser Gwayne.

18:56.052 --> 18:59.221
Look to the sky. To the horizon.

19:00.765 --> 19:02.433
Doom and ruin surround us.

19:05.269 --> 19:07.438
We will all become beasts before our end.

19:08.314 --> 19:10.232
Only if we abandon our principles.

19:18.783 --> 19:20.409
Never knew my mother.

19:23.079 --> 19:25.456
Same as most of the gutter-rats.

19:30.169 --> 19:32.880
Was kicked about more than a mongrel dog.

19:39.136 --> 19:41.597
Wished for death more days
than I wished to live.

19:47.603 --> 19:50.398
There was this priest from Essos.

19:52.525 --> 19:55.778
He fancied me. Paid me coin.

20:00.449 --> 20:01.575
To do things.

20:06.497 --> 20:08.540
He said I had king's blood.

20:08.541 --> 20:10.960
That I was born for a purpose.

20:13.546 --> 20:14.922
I liked that story.

20:16.632 --> 20:17.883
So I owned it.

20:20.094 --> 20:21.762
Ulf the Dragonseed.

20:26.934 --> 20:28.936
And that red cunt was right.

20:33.190 --> 20:34.607
And you?

20:34.608 --> 20:36.694
Where'd you get your dragon's blood?

20:43.284 --> 20:44.535
Did you hear something?

20:47.872 --> 20:49.664
Don't like this place.

20:49.665 --> 20:51.791
All this hanging about.

20:51.792 --> 20:53.626
Vhagar was supposed to be here already.

20:53.627 --> 20:55.211
We have to wait until she comes.

20:55.212 --> 20:57.172
The queen didn't say
nothing about waiting.

20:57.173 --> 20:59.507
She said, come here, kill Aemond.

20:59.508 --> 21:01.594
I wouldn't be too keen to meet Vhagar.

21:02.303 --> 21:04.637
She and the One-Eye have slain
at least two dragons already.

21:04.638 --> 21:06.348
Fight'll be worth it, though.

21:07.600 --> 21:08.768
For the castle.

21:09.852 --> 21:10.853
What castle?

21:11.771 --> 21:14.856
The queen promised to make us knights,

21:14.857 --> 21:16.692
so we get a castle.

21:24.617 --> 21:26.993
- What?
- You have to be named a lord

21:26.994 --> 21:28.161
to get a castle.

21:28.162 --> 21:29.829
- What's a knight get, then?
- A horse.

21:29.830 --> 21:31.831
What do I need with a fucking horse?

21:31.832 --> 21:34.542
- I've got a dragon.
- You'd be Ser Ulf,

21:34.543 --> 21:36.419
and men would have to show you respect.

21:36.420 --> 21:40.382
Men would have to show me respect
'cause of the big fucking dragon.

21:42.384 --> 21:43.761
I can't live in a title.

21:44.637 --> 21:45.805
Or drink it.

21:50.476 --> 21:52.269
I imagine there'd be eager women.

21:54.396 --> 21:56.273
Get more women with a castle.

23:02.131 --> 23:04.592
Did you know Aegon had fled?

23:08.929 --> 23:10.097
He was meant to be here.

23:11.557 --> 23:13.517
It's Aemond who should have flown.

23:14.810 --> 23:15.936
You're frightened.

23:19.732 --> 23:22.151
Ser Criston and Ser Gwayne
are in great peril.

23:23.277 --> 23:24.904
I fear only for our knights.

23:26.989 --> 23:28.364
Aemond should be with them.

23:28.365 --> 23:30.075
Aemond's frightened, too.

23:32.244 --> 23:35.748
After he claimed Vhagar,
he forgot what fear was.

23:36.832 --> 23:38.250
But he remembers now.

23:39.585 --> 23:42.755
He knows that if he has to face
Rhaenyra's dragons, he'll die.

23:52.264 --> 23:53.641
Ser Soren?

23:58.771 --> 24:01.731
Lord Ormund marches here
with the Hightower host.

24:01.732 --> 24:04.985
Dispatch one of your fastest riders
and deliver this to him with haste.

24:05.861 --> 24:07.278
These are the king's instructions.

24:07.279 --> 24:08.405
The king's?

24:10.324 --> 24:12.701
- With haste, Ser Soren.
- At once, Your Grace.

24:16.288 --> 24:17.665
Alyn, sit.

24:37.267 --> 24:38.602
I saved this one.

24:40.980 --> 24:42.147
It's from Ib.

24:43.315 --> 24:45.275
Such luxury is wasted on me.

24:47.653 --> 24:49.279
I've already broken the wax.

24:52.116 --> 24:54.118
And I am not prepared...

24:57.121 --> 24:58.580
to drink alone.

25:15.514 --> 25:18.475
I forget the guttural name
they have for it.

25:20.019 --> 25:22.813
But I believe a rough interpretation
is "dragon water."

25:25.399 --> 25:27.401
An acquired taste, perhaps.

25:29.445 --> 25:30.779
The queen has sent word.

25:32.281 --> 25:34.115
We are to pull five ships
from the blockade,

25:34.116 --> 25:37.035
sail down the Blackwater,
and seize King's Landing's port.

25:37.036 --> 25:38.870
She's taking King's Landing?

25:38.871 --> 25:40.788
Rhaenyra's advantage is now absolute.

25:40.789 --> 25:43.750
She will surround the city
with her dragons

25:43.751 --> 25:45.961
and force the surrender
of Aegon and Aemond.

25:47.337 --> 25:49.465
I admit I know little of this enemy.

25:50.799 --> 25:52.383
But Aemond One-Eye seems the sort

25:52.384 --> 25:54.803
who would sooner let it all burn
than abandon the throne.

25:57.264 --> 25:58.849
Rough seas lie ahead.

26:12.362 --> 26:15.407
I cannot fully mend...

26:16.658 --> 26:20.829
the breach between us.

26:22.331 --> 26:24.541
But I do accept that it was of my making.

26:29.797 --> 26:31.131
I was fond of your mother.

26:33.300 --> 26:34.301
For...

26:35.469 --> 26:36.970
whatever we had together.

26:41.391 --> 26:43.435
I did try to provide a life for you.

26:45.104 --> 26:48.564
- For your brother.
- A life, perhaps.

26:48.565 --> 26:50.025
But never a name.

26:58.450 --> 27:00.035
I am sorry for it.

27:01.870 --> 27:03.413
Sail ho!

27:24.143 --> 27:26.395
Enemy ships sighted!

27:33.402 --> 27:35.820
- Enemy ships sighted.
- What is their strength?

27:35.821 --> 27:37.405
Three-and-fifty counted so far.

27:37.406 --> 27:38.615
They already outnumber us.

27:40.242 --> 27:43.452
Put the oars out.
Send ravens to Dragonstone.

27:43.453 --> 27:45.121
Put the oars out!

27:45.122 --> 27:49.000
Take us to the head of the blockade
and signal the fleet: form battle lines.

27:49.001 --> 27:50.878
Is it the Lannisters or the Greyjoys?

27:51.962 --> 27:53.255
It's the Triarchy.

27:55.757 --> 27:57.509
Bring my armor.

28:20.199 --> 28:21.200
Commander.

28:23.577 --> 28:25.995
The Gullet has three inlets
into the Blackwater,

28:25.996 --> 28:29.874
the largest of which opens
just to the south of Driftmark.

28:29.875 --> 28:33.336
But I hold strongly that we must press
towards the southern inlet.

28:33.337 --> 28:36.881
If our armada engages the Velaryon fleet
at close combat,

28:36.882 --> 28:39.050
it will blunt the threat
of Rhaenyra's dragons.

28:39.051 --> 28:41.427
They will be loath
to burn their own ships.

28:41.428 --> 28:43.013
A canny strategy, my lord.

28:44.056 --> 28:46.642
I can see why your king
made you Lord of the Ships.

28:49.770 --> 28:52.439
You'll rule all this kit
if you wind up in the drink.

28:54.316 --> 28:57.736
My strategy is expressly
not to "end up in the drink."

29:00.489 --> 29:03.450
We will face death on this deck
before we face it in the sea.

29:04.284 --> 29:06.577
You will be glad of our armor
when the fighting starts.

29:06.578 --> 29:08.120
I know I will.

29:08.121 --> 29:11.124
The Sea Snake scouts have
raised the alarm, Commander.

29:12.417 --> 29:14.253
If only to see his face.

29:15.712 --> 29:17.672
Signal Halfjaw to take his detachment

29:17.673 --> 29:19.340
and penetrate the northern pass.

29:19.341 --> 29:21.050
- Mm.
- The northern pass

29:21.051 --> 29:22.385
is the farthest route

29:22.386 --> 29:24.012
running north of Dragonstone.
Whatever for?

29:25.097 --> 29:26.348
To sack High Tide.

29:27.724 --> 29:29.101
Lord Corlys' castle?

29:30.602 --> 29:32.853
We will require
the full strength of your fleet

29:32.854 --> 29:34.772
- if we have any hope--
- High Tide is a monument

29:34.773 --> 29:36.275
to the Sea Snake himself.

29:38.735 --> 29:42.322
Do you think his focus will hold
when he sees his treasure room aflame?

31:05.364 --> 31:08.074
What is the weather to be today, Bold Jon?

31:08.075 --> 31:10.535
Raining piss or shit,
from the looks of the messenger.

31:13.080 --> 31:16.290
Good morrow, ser. What news?

31:16.291 --> 31:17.876
Good morrow, my Lord Hightower.

31:20.379 --> 31:21.922
I bring urgent word from King Aemond.

31:22.798 --> 31:24.049
King, is he now?

31:54.996 --> 31:58.291
Aemond says we have to make camp here
and await further word.

31:59.292 --> 32:01.128
He shall join us in three days' time.

32:07.634 --> 32:09.219
So Aegon's dead, then?

32:13.640 --> 32:15.559
One king is as good as another.

32:16.476 --> 32:18.978
Have this lad bathed and fed.

32:18.979 --> 32:20.856
- Give him a good tent.
- Yes, sire.

32:25.402 --> 32:27.863
Mayhaps the weather will hold.

32:33.577 --> 32:36.037
It is my fault we're in this position.

32:46.840 --> 32:50.051
I strove tirelessly to put Aegon
on the throne, but I...

32:52.345 --> 32:54.264
I failed to prepare him to rule.

32:58.977 --> 33:00.854
His frailties are his own.

33:06.818 --> 33:08.403
You should have been king.

33:12.574 --> 33:14.658
If you'd only been born first,
then perhaps

33:14.659 --> 33:16.536
we wouldn't be here, but...

33:18.497 --> 33:20.582
we must ever play the board before us.

33:31.051 --> 33:35.555
That is why you need to go to Harrenhal.

33:40.685 --> 33:41.852
To what end?

33:41.853 --> 33:43.605
It is a stronghold.

33:44.898 --> 33:47.608
One that has withstood
dragonfire once before.

33:47.609 --> 33:50.362
You are no longer safe here
in King's Landing.

33:58.495 --> 34:00.913
It is well to be fearful.

34:00.914 --> 34:02.415
I, too, am afraid.

34:05.752 --> 34:07.379
I'm not afraid.

34:14.803 --> 34:16.012
Of course not.

34:16.846 --> 34:18.223
But you are the crown now.

34:20.141 --> 34:22.686
And Rhaenyra will send
her new dragons here for you.

34:23.812 --> 34:25.021
Soon or late.

34:28.608 --> 34:30.235
I am not afraid.

34:35.991 --> 34:37.491
Fly to the Riverlands.

34:37.492 --> 34:39.202
Draw Daemon out.

34:40.203 --> 34:43.540
He has just one dragon, and killing him
would be a vicious blow to Rhaenyra.

34:45.709 --> 34:48.587
At Harrenhal, you will be unassailable.

34:53.049 --> 34:54.593
Perhaps I could even meet you there.

34:57.721 --> 34:59.264
That road is uncertain.

35:01.182 --> 35:02.808
But this one,

35:02.809 --> 35:04.893
if you stay here and wait for Rhaenyra

35:04.894 --> 35:08.106
and her dragons to come,
this one is certain.

35:12.819 --> 35:14.404
You are so courageous.

35:16.865 --> 35:18.867
But I cannot lose you as I did Aegon.

35:21.369 --> 35:23.038
If I do, I will be lost.

35:26.291 --> 35:28.627
Heed me, Aemond, please.

36:07.165 --> 36:09.542
I shall host a feast there in your honor.

36:10.752 --> 36:12.379
In Black Harren's hall

36:13.880 --> 36:16.174
whilst my uncle's head
looks down from a spike.

36:44.536 --> 36:45.412
Fuck!

36:47.580 --> 36:50.291
What if Aemond
knew we were coming for him?

36:51.334 --> 36:53.420
He could have attacked
Dragonstone in our absence.

36:54.546 --> 36:57.674
Queen assigned us a task.
We must man it steadfastly.

36:58.800 --> 37:01.136
And if that is what the enemy
is counting upon?

37:11.896 --> 37:13.856
- What is that?
- Fuck this place!

37:13.857 --> 37:16.608
- What's happened?
- I'm leaving is what's happened.

37:16.609 --> 37:18.193
We must wait for Vhagar.

37:18.194 --> 37:20.821
For how long? Forever and a day?

37:20.822 --> 37:22.240
She was meant to be here already.

37:24.367 --> 37:26.326
The queen only instructed us
to ambush Vhagar.

37:26.327 --> 37:28.078
She did not say what to do
if the dragon never came.

37:28.079 --> 37:29.663
I say we remain.

37:29.664 --> 37:31.207
Who made you fucking king?

37:31.833 --> 37:32.916
I don't like it here.

37:32.917 --> 37:34.585
Is that what you'll tell Her Grace?

37:34.586 --> 37:37.337
- That you're craven?
- I'll tell Her Grace true.

37:37.338 --> 37:40.674
That we stood watch and Vhagar never came.

37:40.675 --> 37:42.510
Your friend's right.

37:46.848 --> 37:48.724
You're missing the battle.

37:48.725 --> 37:50.560
The queen needs you at Dragonstone.

37:53.396 --> 37:54.397
Who are you?

37:55.482 --> 37:56.566
I'm a witch.

38:01.821 --> 38:03.448
Right. Look after yourselves.

38:19.547 --> 38:20.840
Your Grace!

38:21.382 --> 38:24.343
- There is war in the Gullet.
- Who?

38:24.344 --> 38:25.636
An armada of ships

38:25.637 --> 38:27.763
sailing out of the rising sun
from the east.

38:27.764 --> 38:29.307
They have sprung their trap.

38:34.896 --> 38:35.939
I shall go.

38:44.113 --> 38:45.240
Mother!

38:45.949 --> 38:47.699
Stop! You cannot!

38:47.700 --> 38:50.410
There is nothing you can say
that I have not heard.

38:50.411 --> 38:51.496
If you die...

38:52.497 --> 38:53.915
Then you will at last be king.

38:56.334 --> 38:57.836
My riding leathers.

39:06.261 --> 39:08.805
You are to lock and bar this door.

39:09.722 --> 39:12.558
The queen must be confined
until she regains her senses.

39:12.559 --> 39:14.643
I could not defy Her Grace's commands.

39:14.644 --> 39:18.022
You are a knight of the Queensguard,
Ser Lorent.

39:19.190 --> 39:22.110
You swore to protect
Her Grace from all threats.

39:23.528 --> 39:25.071
Including herself.

39:30.827 --> 39:31.995
Your life...

39:33.246 --> 39:34.330
for hers.

39:43.256 --> 39:44.756
Jace.

39:44.757 --> 39:46.216
Rescind your command.

39:46.217 --> 39:48.552
- It is treason.
- She has rejected my counsel,

39:48.553 --> 39:50.095
my every attempt to join the fight.

39:50.096 --> 39:52.514
So you make war with her instead?

39:52.515 --> 39:54.975
This is all the work of an ambush,
like Rook's Rest,

39:54.976 --> 39:57.269
a ruse to draw out the queen herself.

39:57.270 --> 40:00.148
They killed my brother, Baela.

40:01.149 --> 40:02.775
I won't let them take her as well.

40:10.450 --> 40:11.826
Come with me.

40:13.703 --> 40:15.496
We are ready.

40:17.123 --> 40:18.666
We can win this victory for her.

40:20.251 --> 40:22.670
Was this not always our purpose?

40:47.612 --> 40:49.988
Ser Lorent, open the door.

40:49.989 --> 40:52.533
Your Grace,
it was the Prince Jacaerys' command.

40:53.743 --> 40:55.118
To ensure your safety.

40:55.119 --> 40:57.245
Open the fucking door.

40:57.246 --> 40:58.122
I cannot.

40:59.332 --> 41:00.875
Ser Lorent!

41:02.585 --> 41:04.087
Jace!

41:07.006 --> 41:08.800
You open the fucking door!

41:10.385 --> 41:12.177
You release me at once!

41:12.178 --> 41:14.389
I will have your heads for this!

41:42.917 --> 41:45.419
Crossbows, ready!

41:45.420 --> 41:46.920
Release!

41:46.921 --> 41:49.340
Archers, ready!

41:50.466 --> 41:51.551
Release!

41:52.260 --> 41:54.511
Archers, ready!

41:54.512 --> 41:56.054
Release!

41:56.055 --> 41:58.557
Barrelman! Signal the fleet:

41:58.558 --> 42:00.267
Do not cluster.

42:00.268 --> 42:01.643
Keep them on the chase.

42:01.644 --> 42:03.603
- Aye-aye!
- The fight is yours.

42:03.604 --> 42:05.230
Archers, ready!

42:05.231 --> 42:07.274
Archers, go!

42:07.275 --> 42:08.358
Loose!

42:08.359 --> 42:10.028
Flagship's been sighted, m'lord.

42:11.070 --> 42:12.320
It's the Bitchfist.

42:12.321 --> 42:13.322
Lohar?

42:16.617 --> 42:18.952
Harden up and make towards her.

42:18.953 --> 42:21.372
- I want her to sight us.
- Aye, m'lord.

42:22.290 --> 42:23.583
Harden up! Pick up the stroke!

42:51.319 --> 42:52.861
Here she comes, lads!

42:52.862 --> 42:55.113
Our jewel in the rough.

42:55.114 --> 42:59.117
Signal the fleet.
The Sea Snake belongs to us.

42:59.118 --> 43:02.204
An equal share of the plunder
when we take the ship!

43:02.205 --> 43:03.748
- Aye, Commander!
- Commander!

43:04.916 --> 43:06.500
Commander!

43:06.501 --> 43:08.293
Ours is the flagship.

43:08.294 --> 43:10.629
We cannot give ourselves
to a singular pursuit.

43:10.630 --> 43:13.049
We must lead the assault
lest it fall into disorder.

43:14.509 --> 43:16.343
Do you think I sailed
across the Narrow Sea

43:16.344 --> 43:18.179
to win your king's war for him?

43:19.847 --> 43:22.183
Those were the terms of the contract.

43:23.434 --> 43:25.685
The Sea Snake led
the persecution and slaughter

43:25.686 --> 43:27.814
of my mates for more than 20 years.

43:29.065 --> 43:30.650
I sealed your contract for him.

43:32.360 --> 43:36.113
Tonight, we shall walk
in the ashes of High Tide!

43:36.114 --> 43:39.282
You'll all join me as I sit
the Driftwood Throne

43:39.283 --> 43:41.369
and dine on the Sea Snake's ears!

43:43.996 --> 43:45.164
Break us free!

43:46.958 --> 43:48.292
And give chase!

44:02.890 --> 44:04.975
He wishes only to protect you.

44:04.976 --> 44:06.727
I never asked to be protected.

44:18.406 --> 44:20.240
I expect it from my council,

44:20.241 --> 44:23.618
those craven men ever clutching
at their doublets.

44:23.619 --> 44:25.036
But my Queensguard?

44:25.037 --> 44:26.497
Mine own son?

45:19.842 --> 45:22.219
I may appear to have the weak
and feeble body of a woman,

45:22.220 --> 45:24.472
but I possess the heart
and spirit of a king.

45:28.267 --> 45:30.352
Enemy to starboard!

45:30.353 --> 45:32.354
- Split, split, split!
- Ballistae, reload!

45:32.355 --> 45:33.856
And put those fires out!

45:36.359 --> 45:38.026
The fleet is surrounded.

45:38.027 --> 45:40.238
And the Bitchfist now pursues us
with a small detachment.

45:41.072 --> 45:42.907
- Dragon!
- Dragon!

45:50.539 --> 45:52.124
Dracarys!

45:56.212 --> 45:57.421
Dracarys!

46:13.729 --> 46:15.856
Set a course through the Dragonstone Pass.

46:17.858 --> 46:20.152
The tide is nearly out.
We'll run aground.

46:21.529 --> 46:24.532
Lohar only wants me. She'll follow.

46:25.658 --> 46:27.868
Without her,
their fleet will be rudderless...

46:28.995 --> 46:30.705
and easy prey for our dragons.

46:34.000 --> 46:35.917
Starboard on our helm!

46:35.918 --> 46:37.752
Fight ready, men!

46:37.753 --> 46:39.630
Bring the grapnels!

46:46.679 --> 46:48.222
- Ready?
- Ready!

46:53.269 --> 46:54.270
Load!

47:25.343 --> 47:28.262
Call me Lohar, Dragon-Slayer!

47:28.971 --> 47:30.348
Press the pursuit!

48:33.494 --> 48:36.121
Ease the sheets and put out the oars.

48:36.122 --> 48:38.123
Cast the leadlines.

48:38.124 --> 48:40.125
Clew up the course.

48:40.126 --> 48:42.460
Leadsmen, to the channels.

48:42.461 --> 48:44.004
Cast the leadline!

48:57.852 --> 49:00.603
Depth, six fathoms!

49:00.604 --> 49:02.397
Barrelman, report!

49:02.398 --> 49:05.066
Breakers dead ahead.

49:05.067 --> 49:07.068
Tide's running hard out.

49:07.069 --> 49:09.447
Currents are strong set to larboard.

49:14.034 --> 49:17.830
Three enemy ships closing fast astern!

49:18.664 --> 49:19.957
Larboard your helm.

49:21.792 --> 49:23.293
Follow my direction closely.

49:23.294 --> 49:26.130
There is a way through the pass,
but it is narrow.

49:27.256 --> 49:30.217
Depth: half-five and fast receding!

49:32.553 --> 49:34.762
- Seven!
- Speed: seven knots!

49:34.763 --> 49:36.556
Slight to larboard.

49:36.557 --> 49:37.933
Aye, Lord Admiral.

49:38.934 --> 49:42.103
- Follow her wake.
- We must go no further.

49:42.104 --> 49:43.814
The pass is too shallow.

49:45.441 --> 49:47.443
We do not know the lay of this place.

49:48.777 --> 49:51.280
- We are sailing blind.
- The Sea Snake will guide us.

49:58.120 --> 50:00.914
- One over four!
- One over four!

50:00.915 --> 50:03.750
Perhaps 70 yards' distance.

50:03.751 --> 50:04.710
Easy now.

50:05.461 --> 50:06.754
Starboard your helm.

50:10.508 --> 50:11.424
Too strong.

50:11.425 --> 50:12.551
Ease it back.

50:19.808 --> 50:20.893
Let me.

50:22.728 --> 50:24.313
Forty yards now.

50:25.523 --> 50:26.607
Thirty-five!

50:27.691 --> 50:30.527
- And a half-three!
- And a half-three!

50:30.528 --> 50:32.362
Bank the oars.

50:32.363 --> 50:34.698
Coxswain ahoy! Bank oars!

50:40.829 --> 50:44.290
- Twenty-five yards!
- Twenty-five yards!

50:44.291 --> 50:46.584
- One over three!
- Ten yards!

50:46.585 --> 50:48.963
- Ten yards!
- We're over the Teeth!

51:11.235 --> 51:12.528
We're clear!

51:21.120 --> 51:23.454
Leave Lohar to the Teeth.

51:23.455 --> 51:26.333
Take us back to the Gullet.
We must rejoin the fight.

52:04.038 --> 52:06.289
Three hands to starboard, now!

52:06.290 --> 52:09.043
- Three hands to starboard!
- We're going to wreck!

52:16.216 --> 52:19.594
We have walked directly into his snare.

52:19.595 --> 52:21.929
Two hands to larboard now
and hold her there!

52:21.930 --> 52:24.599
- Two hands to larboard, hold!
- Cut the anchors!

52:24.600 --> 52:27.226
Drop weight and raise our draft. Quickly!

52:27.227 --> 52:29.563
Aye, Commander! Cut the anchors!

52:34.902 --> 52:36.612
What do you weigh in that armor?

52:40.407 --> 52:42.200
And the rest of them!

52:42.201 --> 52:45.704
Hold that line,
and pull the fucking oars in!

53:04.056 --> 53:07.392
Oars out and close the distance!
Bring the hooks and lines!

53:07.393 --> 53:10.144
Enemy flagship is clear.

53:10.145 --> 53:12.064
She's closing fast astern.

53:13.315 --> 53:15.775
She has the legs on us.
We can't outrun her.

53:15.776 --> 53:17.945
And we've not yet the wind
to carry us against the current.

53:19.488 --> 53:21.656
Furl the sails and put the oars out.

53:21.657 --> 53:23.116
Hard round to starboard.

53:23.117 --> 53:25.368
Ready the offensive
for a broadside assault.

53:25.369 --> 53:28.121
All shields and crossbows,
to your stations!

53:28.122 --> 53:29.748
Load the ballistae!

53:38.757 --> 53:41.635
- Boarding party!
- Boarding party.

53:44.930 --> 53:48.558
Hard about and keep pulling!
Strong against the current.

53:48.559 --> 53:50.602
- Turn!
- Or she'll be dragged back into the Teeth.

54:05.159 --> 54:06.660
She's not turning!

54:11.081 --> 54:12.875
All shields and crossbows to starboard!

54:14.626 --> 54:16.211
Broadside, ready!

54:19.798 --> 54:22.551
Positions, move! Positions!

54:31.477 --> 54:34.020
- Crossbows, ready!
- Ready!

54:34.021 --> 54:35.022
Strike!

54:39.067 --> 54:42.029
Hold that course and fucking row!

54:45.032 --> 54:47.450
Brace and be ready!

54:47.451 --> 54:48.744
Now, strike!

55:02.049 --> 55:03.383
Take the ship.

55:06.428 --> 55:08.889
On your feet! Prepare to engage!

55:30.327 --> 55:31.745
Dracarys!

55:40.546 --> 55:42.214
Bring down the rider!

58:19.788 --> 58:22.123
No! No!

58:22.124 --> 58:24.126
Sheepstealer, no!

58:28.296 --> 58:29.923
That's my sister.

59:47.959 --> 59:48.960
Father!

01:00:05.477 --> 01:00:06.561
Hold on, Baela!

01:00:13.443 --> 01:00:14.444
Rhaena!

01:00:22.869 --> 01:00:24.371
Sheepstealer!

01:00:38.343 --> 01:00:40.720
Sheepstealer! No!

01:00:46.143 --> 01:00:47.144
Vermax!

01:01:00.532 --> 01:01:01.825
Jace!

01:02:07.724 --> 01:02:09.559
Jace!

01:02:17.442 --> 01:02:18.860
Come on, Vermax!
